###  VINTAGE RAZOR BARBERSHOP — API TEST SUITE
###  CMPE 172 Term Project, Spring 2026
###
###  USAGE
###    VS Code:    install the "REST Client" extension, then click
###                "Send Request" above any request block below.
###    IntelliJ:   built-in HTTP client (Run gutter icon).
###
###  ORDER
###    Sections are grouped by purpose. Run from top to bottom on a
###    fresh DB (db/db_init.sql) for the most predictable results.
###
###  DATES
###    The seed script generates 14 days of slots starting tomorrow.
###    Replace dates below with a value within that window — or first
###    call GET /slots and copy a real one from the response.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### SANITY CHECKS
###  Verify the app is up and reachable

### Homepage
GET {{host}}/

### Health check 
###     Expect: 200 OK
GET {{host}}/health

###  BROWSE CATALOG DATA
###  Read-only queries against seed data.
### List all services
###     Expect: 8 services from seed data
GET {{host}}/services

### List available slots — Provider 1 (Lune, Barber)
###     Replace the date with a valid future date in your seed window.
GET {{host}}/slots?providerId=1&date=2026-05-09

### List available slots — Provider 3 (Maelle, Nail Tech)
GET {{host}}/slots?providerId=3&date=2026-05-09

### List slots for an INACTIVE provider (Verso, providerId=5)
###     Expect: empty result — inactive providers have no slots seeded
GET {{host}}/slots?providerId=5&date=2026-05-09

### List slots for an out-of-range date (past or beyond 14 days)
###     Expect: empty result
GET {{host}}/slots?providerId=1&date=2026-01-01



###  BOOKING HAPPY PATH
###  Standard flow: see slots, book, view, cancel, re-book.

### Book a new appointment
###     Replace slotId with one returned from request above.
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "serviceId": 1,
  "slotId": 3,
  "notes": "Standard booking test"
}

### List all appointments
GET {{host}}/appointments

### Cancel an appointment
###     Replace the {id} below with an appointment_id from previous response
PUT {{host}}/appointments/1/cancel

### Re-book the same slot after cancellation
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 2,
  "serviceId": 1,
  "slotId": 3,
  "notes": "Re-booking previously cancelled slot"
}


## CONCURRENCY VERIFICATION
###  Manual race-condition test. 
###  Do two booking simultaneously as possible (different terminals or quick double- click in VS Code). 
### Expected outcome:
###    - One returns 200 OK with appointment details
###    - The other returns 409 Conflict: "Slot X is already booked."


### Concurrent booking — Customer A
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "serviceId": 1,
  "slotId": 5,
  "notes": "Concurrency test — Customer A"
}

### Concurrent booking — Customer B 
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 2,
  "serviceId": 1,
  "slotId": 5,
  "notes": "Concurrency test — Customer B"
}

###  EDGE CASES & ERROR HANDLING
###  Verify the API rejects invalid input cleanly.

### Book with non-existent slotId
###     Expect: 4xx or 5xx error, NOT a silently-created appointment
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "serviceId": 1,
  "slotId": 99999,
  "notes": "Should fail — slot does not exist"
}

### Book with non-existent serviceId
###     Expect: error
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "serviceId": 99999,
  "slotId": 10,
  "notes": "Should fail — service does not exist"
}

### book an already-booked slot (sequential, not concurrent)
###     First book slotId=7 successfully...
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "serviceId": 1,
  "slotId": 7,
  "notes": "First booking — should succeed"
}

### ...then try to book it again
###     Expect: 409 Conflict
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 2,
  "serviceId": 1,
  "slotId": 7,
  "notes": "Second booking — should fail with 409"
}

###  Cancel a non-existent appointment
###     Expect: 4xx error
PUT {{host}}/appointments/99999/cancel

### Cancel an already-cancelled appointment 
###     Replace ID with one cancelled in 3.3.
###     Expect: graceful handling, no crash, appropriate log warning
PUT {{host}}/appointments/1/cancel


###  SYSTEM MANAGEMENT (M6): Metrics and log inspection.

### Booking metrics
###     Expect: success count, failure count, average latency in ms.
###     Counts should reflect everything attempted in this test run.
GET {{host}}/metrics/bookings

### Trigger a successful booking, then re-check metrics
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "serviceId": 2,
  "slotId": 12,
  "notes": "M6 — drives success counter"
}

### Trigger a failed booking, then re-check metrics
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "serviceId": 2,
  "slotId": 99999,
  "notes": "M6 — drives failure counter"
}

### Re-fetch metrics to confirm counters incremented
GET {{host}}/metrics/bookings

### Health check (re-run after load)
###     Demonstrates the endpoint stays responsive under activity.
GET {{host}}/health

###  After running this suite, inspect logs/barbershop.log for:
###    - [BOOKING] SUCCESS / [BOOKING] entries
###    - [CANCEL]  events
###    - [NOTIFICATION CLIENT] / [MOCK NOTIFICATION SERVICE] pairs
###    - WARN-level entries for the conflict and edge-case requests